1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,550
China should have 5 time zones.

2
00:00:02,550 --> 00:00:04,178
It uses one.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,584
It's more than 5,000 km wide,

4
00:00:06,584 --> 00:00:09,896
and the sun takes 4 hours to cross it.

5
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,855
Until 1949, China really had five.

6
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,324
Then the whole country was put on Beijing time.

7
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,022
On a winter morning,

8
00:00:19,022 --> 00:00:21,977
the sun rises over Shanghai before seven.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,600
Then it keeps going west, for hours,

10
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:27,122
until it finally reaches Kashgar,

11
00:00:27,122 --> 00:00:28,565
after 10 a.m.

12
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,381
So many people there quietly keep their own clock,

13
00:00:32,381 --> 00:00:33,845
two hours behind.

14
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,961
One country. One clock.

15
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:40,313
Would you wait until ten for the sunrise?
